      "updated": 1752352803515,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Monster Ideas\n- No hunger\n- Move when player moves (not on player action i.e. using potion)\n- How will damage work?\n    - if the player and monster attempt to move to the same square...?\n- Chance a monster spawns on a level and in a room\n    - additional 1 monster per level?\n    - Iterate over count of spawning zombies, and randomly spawn them in different rooms.\n        - Cannot be the same starting room as the player\n    - Once a player leaves a dark room, random chance a zombie can spawn again. Increase chance as levels increase.\n- Will need to reuse the A* path finding Alg to direct monsters to the player.\n    - Probably only enable this once the player is within (eye sight would be ideal) 10 square radius...for now\n- Monsters should be respawned when going back up stairs. Don't want all the monsters to gather around\n  the stair way when the player runs away, and just waiting there when the player returns.\n- Need to make it so only the monsters on the players current level are attempting to find the player.\n- Need to improve the torch system for corridors. Right now it just has a light up side affect, but the \n  corridor is still discovered one space at a time, which leads to the player suddenly being attacked when\n  the come across a monster.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Monster Ideas\n- No hunger\n- Move when player moves (not on player action i.e. using potion)\n- How will damage work?\n    - if the player and monster attempt to move to the same square...?\n- Chance a monster spawns on a level and in a room\n    - additional 1 monster per level?\n    - Iterate over count of spawning zombies, and randomly spawn them in different rooms.\n        - Cannot be the same starting room as the player\n    - Once a player leaves a dark room, random chance a zombie can spawn again. Increase chance as levels increase.\n- Will need to reuse the A* path finding Alg to direct monsters to the player.\n    - Probably only enable this once the player is within (eye sight would be ideal) 10 square radius...for now\n- Monsters should be respawned when going back up stairs. Don't want all the monsters to gather around\n  the stair way when the player runs away, and just waiting there when the player returns.\n- Need to make it so only the monsters on the players current level are attempting to find the player.\n- Need to improve the torch system for corridors. Right now it just has a light up side affect, but the \n  corridor is still discovered one space at a time, which leads to the player suddenly being attacked when\n  the come across a monster.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
